{
  "name": "How to Plan Your Interior Upgrade Without Stress",
  "step": [
    {
      "name": "Step 1",
      "text": "Planning an interior upgrade doesn't have to be overwhelming. Let's break down the process into manageable steps so you can feel confident and in control. First, during the design and planning phase, clearly define your vision and budget. This is where you decide what you want to change without major structural work. Next, move on to material selection. This is a critical step where you'll want to ask about lead times to avoid future delays. If permits are needed, start researching them during your design phase. Once materials are procured, the installation begins. HH Remodeling LLC manages the carpentry, tile, drywall, and paint, while coordinating other essential sub-trades like plumbing and electrical. Finally, before wrapping up, conduct a thorough punch-list and closeout review to ensure everything meets your expectations. Good planning and clear communication are crucial; HH Remodeling LLC helps keep everything centralized and on track, minimizing rework and ensuring your satisfaction.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 1
    }
  ],
